Today was all about getting hands-on with data cleaning in Power Query Editor. I learned how raw data can be messy, inconsistent, and unreliable—and how important it is to fix that before any analysis.

🔧 Key Concepts Covered
	•	Removing duplicates and unnecessary columns
	•	Handling missing/null values
	•	Changing data types (text, number, date, etc.)
	•	Splitting and merging columns
	•	Renaming columns for clarity
	•	Filtering and sorting data
	•	Using built-in transformations to standardize datasets

💡 What I Learned
Data cleaning is a crucial step in the data analysis process. Clean data ensures:
	•	More accurate insights
	•	Better visualizations
	•	Reliable decision-making

Power Query makes this process efficient and repeatable through its step-by-step transformation system.